<title>CHINA: Macau/Philippines air pact allows direct service.</title>
<headline>Macau/Philippines air pact allows direct service.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Air Macau has flown the first direct flights between the Portugese enclave since the two countries formally signed an air services agreement, a spokesman for Macau International Airport said.</p>
<p>Air Macau flew the first of its twice weekly services between Macau and Manila on Monday July 21 using an Airbus A320 aircraft. The Friday flight uses a slightly larger Airbus A321, the spokesman added.</p>
<p>The new agreement allowed the first aviation link between the two countries to begin. - Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017 - www.racs.com</p>
